  "track": "track-03",
  "title": "query processing execution plans cardinality and parameter sensitivity",
  "status": "source-backed-draft-generation-enabled",
  "concepts": [
    "The optimizer transforms a declarative query into an execution plan using schema, indexes, statistics, parameter information, and cost estimates; a plan is evidence about one compilation and execution context.",
    "Estimated plans show the chosen strategy and estimated rows; actual plans add runtime observations. Differences between estimated and actual cardinality often point to stale or insufficient statistics, data skew, parameter sensitivity, or expression selectivity.",
    "Read plans from data access through joins, filters, sorts, aggregates, and exchanges. Operators are clues, not verdicts: a scan may be correct and cheaper, while a seek can still return too many rows or cause many lookups.",
    "Query Store preserves query and plan history for regression analysis; runtime and wait evidence should accompany plan inspection. Change one factor at a time and measure representative executions.",
    "Parameter-sensitive plan optimization and other intelligent query processing features evolve by SQL Server release and configuration; distinguish automatic behavior from deliberate query hints."
  ],
