  "accuracyFacts": [
    "An estimated plan contains optimizer estimates but no actual execution measurements; an actual plan records runtime observations from one execution and is not representative of all parameter values.",
    "Operator icons are not diagnoses: compare estimated and actual rows, executions, rows read, predicates, memory and waits; a seek can still read a broad range or incur repeated lookups.",
    "PSP currently works with eligible equality predicates. SQL Server 2025 at compatibility level 170 adds eligible DML and multi-predicate same-table support, but selected predicates remain capped at three; range combinations can yield more than three variants.",
    "OPPO requires compatibility level 170, OPTIONAL_PARAMETER_OPTIMIZATION enabled, and a qualifying optional-NULL predicate. Its dispatcher and skipped-reason events differ from PSP diagnostics.",
    "CE feedback for expressions is SQL Server 2025 compatibility 160 on SQL Server and 170 on Azure SQL Database. DOP feedback and persisted memory-grant feedback depend on Query Store configuration and eligibility.",
    "Query Store is enabled by default for new SQL Server 2022+ databases in READ_WRITE mode, not for all existing databases or prior versions. Runtime statistics are aggregated by intervals and capture/capacity state can create history gaps.",
    "Query Store for readable secondary replicas is preview; SQL Server 2025 must enable it per database and uses replica_group_id for runtime attribution and scoped hints. PSP readable-secondary access violation was resolved in SQL Server 2025 CU1.",
    "Query Store hints can override statement and plan-guide hints, but unsupported/contradictory hints may be ignored; ABORT_QUERY_EXECUTION is the exception that prevents execution. Verify application/failure status and retire stale interventions."
  ]
